    <div class="prose max-w-none">
      <p>
    I obtained my PhD <i>(Cum Laude)</i> in the <a href="https://www.phd-ai.it/"target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National PhD Programme in Artificial Intelligence</a> at the Polytechnic of Turin, under the supervision of Prof. <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=LbgTPRwAAAAJ&hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Marco Cristani</a> and Prof. <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=KHAIAA8AAAAJ&hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Alessandro Farinelli</a>.


<!-- At present, I am a Applied Scientist Intern at Amazon in Madrid!

Previously, I spent five months as a Visiting Student Researcher at Simon Fraser University (Vancouver, Canada), where I worked under the supervision of Prof. Angel Xuan Chang in the GrUVi lab. -->
      </p>
      <!-- <p>My research interests broadly lie in Deep Learning, with a particular focus on enhancing the autonomy of intelligent agents. Currently, I am exploring Foundation Models (VLMs, LLMs & VLAs) and their applications in Embodied AI, with the goal of advancing navigation, embodied reasoning, and human-robot interaction.
    </p> -->

    <p>
      My research follows three main directions: (i) leveraging VLMs/VLAs for spatial reasoning in navigation; (ii) uncertainty-aware navigation and human-agent interaction for handling instruction ambiguity; and (iii) neural scene representations for language-grounded perception. <br>
      My work has appeared in top-tier venues including ICCV, TPAMI, and IROS, with all code publicly available. 
      I am particularly interested in bridging foundation models with real-world robotic systems.
    </p>
